 "sentences": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.54,
   "n_words": 15,
   "text": "He loaded the shotgun with gold and fired it into the walls of the mine."
  },
  {
   "start": 3.76,
   "end": 6.36,
   "n_words": 10,
   "text": "His buddy just watches the gold vanish into the rock."
  },
  {
   "start": 6.7,
   "end": 8.92,
   "n_words": 8,
   "text": "So we're shooting gold into a gold mine?"
  },
  {
   "start": 9.12,
   "end": 10.58,
   "n_words": 5,
   "text": "You see, it's called salting."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.74,
   "end": 13.76,
   "n_words": 12,
   "text": "He's dug this mine for 10 years and found nothing but rock."
  },
  {
   "start": 13.92,
   "end": 16.02,
   "n_words": 10,
   "text": "And tomorrow, a rich guy is coming to buy it."
  },
  {
   "start": 16.1,
   "end": 18.7,
   "n_words": 11,
   "text": "So he spent his last hundred bucks on gold dust instead."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.94,
   "end": 23.18,
   "n_words": 19,
   "text": "Next morning, the rich guy rolls up in a white suit and bangs his head on the first beam."
  },
  {
   "start": 23.34,
   "end": 25.82,
   "n_words": 10,
   "text": "But he's brought an expert, and the expert isn't stupid."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.82,
   "end": 30.46,
   "n_words": 18,
   "text": "He smashes a chunk of wall, swirls it in a pan, and gold flakes spin to the bottom."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.64,
   "end": 33.38,
   "n_words": 9,
   "text": "But under his magnifying glass, every flake is flat."
  },
  {
   "start": 33.66,
   "end": 35.52,
   "n_words": 7,
   "text": "Somebody shot this gold into the wall."
  },
  {
   "start": 35.7,
   "end": 36.94,
   "n_words": 6,
   "text": "But the rich guy just laughs."
  },
  {
   "start": 37.3,
   "end": 39.44,
   "n_words": 8,
   "text": "Why would anyone shoot gold into a wall?"
  },
  {
   "start": 39.58,
   "end": 40.22,
   "n_words": 2,
   "text": "That's insane!"
  },
  {
   "start": 40.5,
   "end": 41.34,
   "n_words": 4,
   "text": "And his buddy nods."
  },
  {
   "start": 42.04,
   "end": 42.76,
   "n_words": 2,
   "text": "Completely insane."
  },
  {
   "start": 43.08,
   "end": 49.1,
   "n_words": 27,
   "text": "So the rich guy pays up, and while those two bolt with the money, he stays behind and pulls a stick of dynamite out of his suit."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.22,
   "end": 51.02,
   "n_words": 8,
   "text": "He's never mind a day in his life."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.18,
   "end": 54.74,
   "n_words": 15,
   "text": "So he just lights it, tosses it down the tunnel like a firecracker, and runs."
  },
  {
   "start": 54.74,
   "end": 60.94,
   "n_words": 25,
   "text": "And when the dust clears, there's a vein of real gold as thick as your arm, 10 feet past where the last guy gave up."
  }
 ]
